Findings
F12 [Major]: Both session-create bodies send directory instead of location.directory.
The live handler defaults this request to process.cwd(). That directory is /home/daniebo.
The job-root deny config therefore does not protect the created session.
L1 and L11 assert the same incorrect shape.

F13 [Major]: Review calls use a zero wait, although the prompt endpoint admits input asynchronously.
An empty answer produces a complete pass with a zero-byte output after one GET.
A partial answer also produces complete. The judge stops at the first text part.
Use one deadline and await terminal completion.

F14 [Major]: The live synthesizers discard native tokens beside content.
The native completed-answer fixture records all token fields as zero and tokens_complete false.
L4 supplies invented step_finish content instead of the native token shape.

F15 [Major]: Neither scheduled driver nor transient service unit sets BENCH_SERVER_BASE.
The user manager also has no value for it.
The runner silently selects isolated seeding for pilot routes without that variable.
Configure the caller and refuse that fallback for pilots.

F16 [Major]: Both wait helpers capture the status after shell negation.
A failed GET therefore returns status zero. Both extracted-function fixtures reproduce it.

F17 [Major]: Native assistant errors disappear during synthesis.
A native region error produces a complete pass and an empty output instead of region-blocked.

F18 [Major]: The URL guard accepts http://127.0.0.1:38307@example.invalid.
The actual hostname is example.invalid. The extracted guard selects LIVE_PATH=1.
No request ran during this proof.

F19 [Nit]: L2 omits missing and unreadable config cases.
L5 omits the exact timeout line and exit code. L7 exercises only a pass.
The missing-config behavior also differs from the strategy's refusal requirement.

