No repository test file changed. The helpers used synthetic temporary fixtures and fake servers.
Every fixture made one message GET and returned exit zero with one complete pass record.
- Missing answer: zero-byte output; zero tokens; tokens_complete false.
- Native completed answer: native token values 7, 8, 9, 10, and 11 all became zero.
- Native partial answer: no completed time or finish; the runner stored the partial output.
- Native region error: zero-byte output; the error never reached classification.

Both actual synthesizers also discarded native tokens in an independent in-memory evaluation.
Both wait helpers returned zero when their GET helper returned one.
The wait helper returned immediately on one text count with a 600-second budget.
Each HTTP request also receives a fresh timeout instead of sharing one call deadline.

